commit_template_hash: 686bd6f6d3f60a9716f8ca85195b61c4852e2e6d8a91cf7a01fc867d6252a9af
intent: Fix a real lease leak in the nool_try arm: nool propose --try-branch takes out its own lease independent of the harness's admission lease (already known -- _discard_and_release cleans it up on rejection), but nothing released it on a SUCCESSFUL promote. Discovered running the N=10/v3 ladder point with real cluster contention (corpus v3's up-to-5-ticket same-footprint clusters, which the smaller v1 8-ticket smoke corpus never exercises): rep 1 landed only 50/60 -- 6 of the 10 misses were 'Coordination conflict' rejections where a ticket properly admitted on its own declared footprint got refused by propose because an EARLIER, ALREADY-PROMOTED cluster-mate's leaked propose-lease on that same file was still outstanding. Fixed by releasing --all --agent-id after a successful promote too, mirroring the rejection path. The confounded 50/60 result was never landed (still in the working tree) and is discarded in favor of a clean rerun with this fix
knot_id: 901c6f28d1c5fa9f2c54ee4590c549742ca4988a696ec08a2bbaee3db20ec760
